WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.100
Hey this is Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:07.866
There's a math problem that's gone viral
on Instagram with over 6 million views.

00:00:07.933 --> 00:00:10.200
I'll read the question out for you.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.733
There's a negative sign.

00:00:11.733 --> 00:00:14.733
Then 9 squared plus 81.

00:00:14.966 --> 00:00:17.500
What's the correct answer?

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.933
Tens of thousands of people are arguing

00:00:19.933 --> 00:00:22.933
whether the correct answer is 162.

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:25.833
Or the correct answer is 0.

00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:28.000
What do you think?

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.066
In this video,
I'm going to explain the correct answer

00:00:31.066 --> 00:00:35.500
according to the modern interpretation
of the order of operations.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:40.200
Under that interpretation,
the correct answer is zero.

00:00:40.266 --> 00:00:41.900
I'm going to explain why.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:46.733
We can remember the order of operations
by the acronyms PEMDAS or BODMAS.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.900
This refers to parentheses/brackets,
exponents/orders,

00:00:50.066 --> 00:00:53.066
multiplication and division,
and addition and subtraction.

00:00:53.233 --> 00:00:57.366
If you have two operators of the same
precedence, evaluate from left to right.

00:00:57.366 --> 00:01:01.866
In this expression,
we first evaluate the exponent.

00:01:01.933 --> 00:01:08.200
So we have 9 squared, which is equal to
9 times 9, which equals 81.

00:01:08.266 --> 00:01:11.766
We then have the opposite of 81 plus 81.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:15.966
So we have an addition
and that's equal to 0.

00:01:16.033 --> 00:01:19.400
And that's the correct answer.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.766
Just for further illustration,

00:01:21.766 --> 00:01:25.733
you could type this expression into Google
and it will show you

00:01:25.766 --> 00:01:30.733
that the opposite of 9 squared
plus 81 is equal to 0.

00:01:30.833 --> 00:01:36.000
And Google will even parse [it] out,
so you see a parentheses around 9 squared

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.600
so it's evaluated first.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.600
And then you take the opposite
of 9 squared.

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:45.600
So the opposite of 9 squared
plus 81 is equal to 0.

00:01:45.666 --> 00:01:49.133
But if you don't trust Google,
you could even type this into Wolfram

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:52.866
Alpha, which will show you
the opposite of 9 squared plus

00:01:52.866 --> 00:01:55.866
81 is equal to 0.

00:01:55.933 --> 00:01:58.366
Zero is the correct answer.

00:01:58.366 --> 00:02:04.333
Zip, zilch, nada, शून्य (sunya),
squadoosh!

00:02:04.433 --> 00:02:08.233
Now, if you didn't get this,
there is widespread misunderstanding

00:02:08.233 --> 00:02:10.300
about this concept.

00:02:10.366 --> 00:02:11.066
Several years

00:02:11.066 --> 00:02:16.400
ago, a study of prospective elementary
teachers showed that they incorrectly

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:21.466
applied the order of operations
to compute the opposite of 3 squared.

00:02:21.566 --> 00:02:23.800
So it's not just students
who get this wrong,

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:28.466
but even sometimes teachers
don't evaluate this correctly.

00:02:28.533 --> 00:02:30.633
To further illustrate the point,

00:02:30.633 --> 00:02:35.700
here's a clip from a textbook
that shows that the opposite of 3 squared

00:02:35.733 --> 00:02:41.433
is evaluated as the opposite of 3 times
3, which equals -9.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:45.700
This is definitely the way
that it's understood in mathematics.

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.233
So why does this matter?

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:51.566
Let's say you have a function f(x)
is equal to the opposite of x squared.

00:02:51.633 --> 00:02:56.133
If you were to graph this,
it would be a parabola pointing downward.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:59.033
Now f of nine would be equal
to the opposite

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:02.400
of nine squared, which is equal to -81.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:06.300
It is not equal to positive 81.

00:03:06.366 --> 00:03:09.733
So you have the point nine come in -81.

00:03:09.833 --> 00:03:12.833
The concept even applies in higher
mathematics.

00:03:12.966 --> 00:03:15.966
Here's
an equation for the standard normal curve.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:19.200
So you would take the opposite
of z squared here.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.933
And the standard normal curve
will look something like this.

00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:26.666
So the opposite of 9 squared
plus 81 is equal to 0.

00:03:26.833 --> 00:03:31.533
And I hope that we can end this widespread
misunderstanding.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:34.600
Thanks for making us
one of the best communities on YouTube.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:38.200
See you next episode of Mind
Your Decisions where we solve the world's

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.266
problems, one video at a time.

